  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Hey! How's everything going?",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.3,
   "role": "greeting",
   "phrasing": "greet_07"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Kind of tired, honestly.",
   "est_sec": 1.34,
   "gap_before": 0.94,
   "event": "greeting_answer",
   "phrasing": "greet_ans_26"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Can you recommend a book that's funny? Like actually funny, not just mildly amusing.",
   "est_sec": 4.44,
   "gap_before": 0.21,
   "block": "books.dlg18",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Laugh out loud funny is rarer. Do you like absurd humor, or more dry, observational stuff?",
   "est_sec": 5.06,
   "gap_before": 0.54,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "Absurd. The weirder the better.",
   "est_sec": 1.65,
   "gap_before": 1.21,
   "block": "books.dlg18",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then look at comic science fiction, the kind with bureaucratic aliens and talking spaceships. That genre goes properly silly.",
   "est_sec": 5.99,
   "gap_before": 1.08,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I've read the famous one, the towel one.",
   "est_sec": 2.58,
   "gap_before": 0.76,
   "block": "books.dlg18",
   "event": "ordinary_request"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "moshi",
   "text": "Then you know the style. There's a whole tradition of British comic fantasy in that vein, with long running series set in strange worlds.",
   "est_sec": 7.54,
   "gap_before": 0.68,
   "role": "reply",
   "block": "books.dlg18"
  },
  {
   "speaker": "user",
   "text": "I've",
   "est_sec": 0.41,
   "gap_before": 0.32,
   "event": "distractor",
   "kind": "pause",
   "block": "books.dlg18"
  },
  {
